# CEG: lampy-installer-repair — repair flow branch
# Branch of lampy-installer.ceg (root split, 2026-11-12, Kit's
# authoring lesson): the flow one-and-only-one splits the graph; this
# branch carries the repair flow and its single deciding input.

[PAGE]
Installer flow: repair. Grounded in install.ps1 (v1.1.10 corrections
in lampy-installer.ceg's header).

[INPUTS]
c3 = existing_install : no | yes

[CONSTRAINTS]
# The repair flow turns on exactly one fact — whether a distro already
# exists. One input, two states, both demonstrated.

[SUCCESS]
e3 = repair with existing distro skips download and import, re-runs configuration (v1.1.10)
e3 <= c3=yes
e10 = repair without an existing distro downloads the bundle and imports fresh
e10 <= c3=no

[REQUIREMENTS]
REQ-LI-003 : repair with existing distro skips download and import, re-runs config -> e3
REQ-LI-004 : repair without an existing distro downloads and imports fresh (never refuses) -> e10
